<title>GERMANY: Pan-German May adjusted jobless rises 56,000.</title>
<headline>Pan-German May adjusted jobless rises 56,000.</headline>
<dateline>NUREMBERG, Germany 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Labour Office reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN UNEMPLOYMENT   May 97	Apr 97	   May 96</p>
<p> Number (unadj)		4.256 mln   4.347 mln	3.818 mln</p>
<p> Number (adj)		  4.358 mln   4.302 mln	3.921 mln</p>
<p> Change in adj number	+56,000     +9,000	   n/a</p>
<p> Rate (unadj)		  11.1 pct    11.3 pct	 10.0 pct</p>
<p> Short-time workers	  183,126     238,796	  302,556</p>
<p> Vacancies (unadj)	   360,628     363,261	  363,407</p>
<p> Change in numbers in work Mar 97	Feb 97</p>
<p>				   +42,000     -47,000</p>
<p>NOTE - Numbers in work data refer to change from previous month. Details on numbers in work to be released later today.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
